1. d4 Nf6 2. c4 g6 3. Nc3 d5 4. cxd5 Nxd5 5. e4 Nxc3 6. bxc3 c5 7. Bc4 Bg7 8.
Ne2 O-O 9. O-O Qc7 10. d5 Nd7 11. f4 Nb6 12. Bd3 f5 13. a4 fxe4 14. Bxe4 Bg4
15. a5 Nc4 16. Bd3 Nd6 17. Bd2 c4 18. Bc2 Qc5+ {"Black has won the opening . .
. Mr James is a veteran amateur who has done great work in organizing but
Griffiths is more, a British Championship aspirant and an international. He
proceeds to demonstrate the fact that chess offers scope not only for pure
skill but also for steadiness and deter­mination. Unfortunately we have used
up so much of our space on the opening that we have not enough left to do
justice to Griffiths’s magnificent fight back." (BH Wood, ILN)} 19. Rf2 Qxd5
20. h3 Bf5 21. Ng3 Bxc2 22. Qxc2 Nf5 23. Ne4 b6 24. a6 Qd3 25. Qxd3 cxd3 26. g4
Nd4 $2 27. cxd4 Bxd4 28. Ra3 Rfd8 29. Kf1 Bxf2 30. Nxf2 Rac8 31. Rxd3 Rxd3 32.
Nxd3 e6 33. Ke2 Rc4 34. Ke3 Ra4 35. Nb4 Kf7 36. Kd4 Ke7 37. Kc4 Ra3 38. Kb5 Kd7
39. Nc6 Rb3+ 40. Bb4 Rxh3 41. Nxa7 Kc7 42. Nc6 Rd3 43. Kc4 Rf3 44. Nd8 Rxf4+
45. Kb5 Rf1 46. Nxe6+ Kb8 47. Kxb6 Rf6 48. Bd6+ {"Lucky win after that
opening!" (Griffiths or Tapper) Sources: PC Griffiths scorebooks (input by
Matthew Tapper); Illustrated London News, 11 May 1968} 1-0

